<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Syriza</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">2004</span> · <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a> · Also known as Coalition of the Radical Left</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Syriza, the Coalition of the Radical Left, is a Greek left-wing party formed as an electoral alliance in 2004 and as a single party in 2012. Led by Alexis Tsipras, it won the elections of January 2015 on a promise to end austerity, but after a referendum rejected the creditors' terms it accepted a third bailout that summer. It governed until 2019.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/syriza.jpg" alt="Syriza" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: ThecentreCZ · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_SYRIZA.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
